<p>Note: The company said mild weather during the quarter reduced kWh sales to residential and commercial customers at TNP's principal subsidiary, Texas-New Mexico Power Co.</p>
<p>In addition, earnings per share were diluted by the issuance of two million shares of common stock in October 1996.</p>
<p>The company said that despite the mild weather, earnings at TNMP increased to $9.4 million during the quarter compared to $8.0 million for the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>The increase in earnings at TNMP was offset by net operating losses of $1.4 million at Facility Works, the company's wholly-owned, non-regulated subsidiary.</p>
